Article 159 (Joint penalty provisions) Where the representative of a corporation, or an agent or employee of, or other persons employed by, a corporation or an individual commits any violations described in Articles 148, 148-2, and 149 through 157 in connection with the business affairs of the corporation or the individual, the corporation or individual shall, in addition to punishing the violators accordingly, be subject to a fine or minor fine prescribed in the relevant Article; provided, this shall not apply to cases where such corporation or individual has not been negligent in giving due attention and supervision concerning the relevant business affairs to prevent such violations.
