ADDENDA <Act No. 20270, Feb. 13, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to grounds for disqualification of traffic safety education instructors, instructors of specialized driving schools, and skill examiners)
The amended provisions of Articles 76 (3) 2 (b), (c), and (d), 106 (3) 1, and 107 (3) 2 shall begin to apply to persons punished for a criminal act committed after this Act enters into force; provided, the previous provisions shall apply to those who violate Article 3 (1) of the Act on Special Cases concerning the Settlement of Traffic Accidents or Article 5-3 of the Act on the Aggravated Punishment of Specific Crimes.
Article 3 (Applicability to revocation and suspension of drivers' licenses)
The amended provisions of Article 93 (1) 11 shall begin to apply where a person who has obtained a driver's license commits a crime prescribed in Articles 8 through 10 of the Special Act on Prevention of Insurance Fraud by using a motor vehicle, etc. as a tool or place for crime after this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning dispositions to revoke qualification of instructors of specialized driving schools and skill examiners)
The previous provisions shall apply to the disposition to revoke qualification for criminal acts committed before this Act enters into force.

